# A fleet of three, for the first day on hardware.
#
# Competence is what the manifest says a member's judgment is worth, on a
# scale of 1 to 100 (D24). Whoever assembles the fleet decides what it
# measures and normalises onto the scale: the square root of a language
# model's parameter count adjusted for quantisation, a benchmark score, an
# instrument's calibration record, or the agreement history of a
# deterministic calculation. The protocol never learns which.
#
# The ratio cap is 3:1, so scoring every member into 34..100 keeps any
# manifest lawful however the members are scored one by one.

version 1
epoch 1

# These three come from the worked example in HANDOFF.md: parameter counts
# of 8 B, 3 B and 0.5 B, square-rooted and mapped onto 34..100.
member 0 100 ship-alpha
member 1 66 ship-bravo
member 2 34 ship-charlie
